            "columns_description" :
              [
                "Includes sum of Murder, Rape, Robbery, Aggravated\nAssault, Burglary, Larceny and Motor Vehicle Theft.",
                "One count per victim. The unlawful taking, carrying,\nleading, or riding away of property from the possession or\nconstructive possession of another. It includes crimes such\nas shoplifting, purse snatching, bicycle thefts, etc., in which\nno use of force, violence, or fraud occurs. This offense\ncategory does not include offenses such as embezzlement,\nforgery, or bad checks.",
                "Year the crime incident was reported.",
                "Police Department that reported the crime.",
                "One count per victim. The theft or attempted theft of a\nmotor vehicle, including automobiles, trucks, buses,\nmotorcycles, and snowmobiles.",
                "Subtotal includes Burglary, Larceny and Motor\nVehicle Theft.",
                "One count per victim. The unlawful attack by one person\nupon another for the purpose of inflicting severe or\naggravated bodily injury. This type of assault is usually\naccompanied by the use of a weapon or by means likely to\nproduce death or great bodily harm, and also includes\nattempts to commit murder.",
                "Subtotal includes Murder, Rape, Robbery and\nAggravated Assault.",
                "Location where the crime was reported.",
                "Region where the crime was reported. Regions include\nNew York City (Bronx, Kings, New York, Queens, and\nRichmond counties) and Non-New York City (all other\ncounties).",
                "One count per victim. The taking or attempting to take\nanything of value from the care, custody, or control of a\nperson or persons by force or threat of force or violence\nand/or by putting the victim in fear.",
                "One count per victim. The unlawful entry of a structure to\ncommit a felony or theft. The use of force to gain entry is\nnot required to classify an offense as Burglary.",
                "Number of months an individual agency reported for the\nyear.",
                "One count per victim. The willful killing of one human\nbeing by another. Excludes deaths caused by negligence,\nsuicide, or justifiable homicides, and attempts to murder,\nwhich are classified as assault.",
                "One count per victim. Penetration, no matter how slight, of the vagina or anus with any body part or object, or oral penetration by a sex organ of another person, without the consent of the victim."
